---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---
<Layout title="About" description="About the Peptide Rulebook: mission, methodology, and editorial approach." canonical="/about">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About', href: '/about' }]} />
    <div class="py-10 prose max-w-none">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-ink">About Peptide Rulebook</h1>
      <p class="lead">Peptide Rulebook is a source-linked reference for the regulatory status of peptides in the United States and selected other jurisdictions.</p>
      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Track FDA approval, compounding, shortage, and enforcement status.</li>
        <li>Explain the rules that determine whether a peptide can be approved, compounded, marketed, or sold.</li>
        <li>Check common claims against controlling sources.</li>
        <li>Publish updates when rules or statuses change.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide legal, medical, or compliance advice for a specific product or situation.</li>
        <li>Accept payment to change a status or ranking.</li>
        <li>Replace official agency guidance or a qualified professional.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
      <p>We do not accept sponsored status changes, paid placement, or advertising that influences editorial conclusions. Funding and conflicts are disclosed on our <a href="/about/funding">funding page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
